# Normalize all text to LF in the index so a generator's committed output is one byte shape
# on every platform — otherwise a Windows `newline=None` write (CRLF) drifts against a CI
# `git diff --exit-code` run on Linux, and only a local `core.autocrlf` hides it.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF — CRLF breaks the `#!` shebang on Linux deploy boxes.
*.sh text eol=lf

# ALWAYS diff source, whatever the content sniffer decides. One NUL byte — used as a key
# separator inside a template literal — made git call a whole hook file binary, so it stat-lined
# as `Bin 13089 -> 14743` and no reviewer ever saw the line that broke the app. `gate.py`'s
# `undiffable` check refuses the byte; this makes the diff readable even when one gets in.
*.py diff
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
